IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- INSTRUMENT: Telecommunications (Dealers) Regulations (Cap. 323, Rg 6), 2004 Revised Edition: regulations 3 to 25 and the
-- five Schedules, other than the parts in sgta-i-rg6-dealers.l4 (reg 2 definitions, reg 20(1) and (2), reg 22, Fifth Schedule item 3).
-- Text: subjects/sg/telecommunications-dealers-regulations-2003/registers/source-bundle/TA1999-RG6.txt.
-- A dealer is a person who manufactures, imports for sale, lets for hire, sells, or offers or possesses for sale telecommunication equipment.
-- Each rule answers what the regulation lets the Authority do, or requires of a dealer or other person.  What S 478/2005, S 396/2007,
-- S 210/2010, S 178/2011, S 251/2013, S 414/2014 and S 725/2014 change is in sgta-i-rg6-amendments.l4.

§ `Rg 6 regulation 3: Dealer's Class Licence`

-- src:TA1999-RG6:104 | 3. —(1) Subject to regulation 7, a dealer who manufactures, imports, lets for hire, sells,
-- src:TA1999-RG6:105 | or offers or possesses for sale any type-approved equipment, registered equipment or
-- src:TA1999-RG6:106 | telecommunication equipment set out in the First Schedule shall be deemed to have been
-- src:TA1999-RG6:107 | granted a Dealer’s Class Licence under section 5 of the Act for that purpose.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:108 | (2) The holder of a Dealer’s Class Licence shall, in addition to any requirement imposed
-- src:TA1999-RG6:109 | under these Regulations, comply with the conditions of that licence set out in the Second
-- src:TA1999-RG6:110 | Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:111 | (3) The Authority may impose any condition in addition to those referred to in
-- src:TA1999-RG6:112 | paragraph (2) and may vary or waive all or any of such conditions.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:113 | (4) The holder of a Dealer’s Class Licence shall, at his own expense, comply with the
-- src:TA1999-RG6:114 | varied or additional conditions referred to in paragraph (3).
-- src:TA1999-RG6:115 | (5) The holder of a Dealer’s Class Licence shall register with the Authority in such form
-- src:TA1999-RG6:116 | as the Authority may determine each of the premises under his control or occupation
-- src:TA1999-RG6:117 | where he manufactures, imports, lets for hire, sells, or offers or possesses for sale any
-- src:TA1999-RG6:118 | type-approved equipment, registered equipment or telecommunication equipment set out
-- src:TA1999-RG6:119 | in the First Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:120 | (6) The Authority shall acknowledge the registration under paragraph (5) to the licensee
-- src:TA1999-RG6:121 | and the acknowledgment shall be in such form as the Authority may determine.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:122 | (7) For the purposes of paragraph (5), the holder of a Dealer’s Class Licence shall
-- src:TA1999-RG6:123 | submit in writing to the Authority such information as the Authority may require relating
-- src:TA1999-RG6:124 | to his particulars and the description and scope of his dealings in telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG6:125 | equipment.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:126 | (8) The holder of a Dealer’s Class Licence shall furnish the Authority with such
-- src:TA1999-RG6:127 | specifications and information as the Authority may require on the types of
-- src:TA1999-RG6:128 | telecommunication equipment manufactured, sold or to be manufactured or sold by him.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:129 | (9) The holder of a Dealer’s Class Licence shall notify the Authority of any change in
-- src:TA1999-RG6:130 | any particular furnished to the Authority under this regulation within 14 days of such
-- src:TA1999-RG6:131 | change.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:132 | (10) No person shall furnish any false, misleading or inaccurate information to the
-- src:TA1999-RG6:133 | Authority under this regulation.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:134 | (11) Where the holder of a Dealer’s Class Licence ceases to manufacture, import, let for
-- src:TA1999-RG6:135 | hire, sell, or offer or possess for sale any type-approved equipment, registered equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6:136 | or telecommunication equipment set out in the First Schedule, the holder shall inform the
-- src:TA1999-RG6:137 | Authority of such cessation as soon as practicable.
@ref Rg 6 reg 3 (src:TA1999-RG6:104-137)
GIVEN `the dealer is not excluded by regulation 7` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dealer manufactures, imports, lets for hire, sells, or offers or possesses for sale type-approved equipment, registered equipment or equipment set out in the First Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 3(1): the dealer is deemed to have been granted a Dealer's Class Licence under section 5 of the Act` MEANS
    `the dealer is not excluded by regulation 7` AND `the dealer manufactures, imports, lets for hire, sells, or offers or possesses for sale type-approved equipment, registered equipment or equipment set out in the First Schedule`

GIVEN `the holder complies with the conditions in the Second Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder complies, at its own expense, with the varied or additional conditions the Authority imposed or varied under paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 3(2) to (4): the holder of a Dealer's Class Licence is meeting the conditions` MEANS
    `the holder complies with the conditions in the Second Schedule` AND `the holder complies, at its own expense, with the varied or additional conditions the Authority imposed or varied under paragraph (3)`

GIVEN `the holder registered with the Authority, in the form it determined, each of the premises under its control or occupation where it deals in such equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder submitted the information the Authority required about its particulars and the description and scope of its dealings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder furnished the specifications and information the Authority required on the types of equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days after a change in any particular furnished, that the holder notified the Authority` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 3(5), (7), (8) and (9): the holder has done what the regulation requires` MEANS
        `the holder registered with the Authority, in the form it determined, each of the premises under its control or occupation where it deals in such equipment`
    AND `the holder submitted the information the Authority required about its particulars and the description and scope of its dealings`
    AND `the holder furnished the specifications and information the Authority required on the types of equipment`
    AND (`days after a change in any particular furnished, that the holder notified the Authority` AT MOST 14)

GIVEN `the person furnishes false, misleading or inaccurate information to the Authority under the regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 3(10): the person has breached the regulation` MEANS
    `the person furnishes false, misleading or inaccurate information to the Authority under the regulation`

GIVEN `the holder ceased to deal in such equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder informed the Authority of the cessation as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 3(11): the holder has done what the regulation requires on ceasing to deal` MEANS
    (NOT `the holder ceased to deal in such equipment`) OR `the holder informed the Authority of the cessation as soon as practicable`

§ `Rg 6 regulation 4: Dealer's Individual Licence`

-- src:TA1999-RG6:140 | 4. —(1) A dealer who wishes to manufacture, import, let for hire, sell, or offer or
-- src:TA1999-RG6:141 | possess for sale any telecommunication equipment that is not —
-- src:TA1999-RG6:142 | (a) type-approved equipment;
-- src:TA1999-RG6:143 | (b) registered equipment; or
-- src:TA1999-RG6:144 | (c) telecommunication equipment set out in the First Schedule,
-- src:TA1999-RG6:145 | shall obtain a Dealer’s Individual Licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:146 | (2) Every application for a Dealer’s Individual Licence shall be made in such form and
-- src:TA1999-RG6:147 | manner as the Authority may, from time to time, determine and shall be supported by
-- src:TA1999-RG6:148 | such information as the Authority may require.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:149 | (3) No person shall furnish any false, misleading or inaccurate information for the
-- src:TA1999-RG6:150 | purpose of obtaining a Dealer’s Individual Licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:151 | (4) The Authority shall notify the applicant as to whether his application is successful
-- src:TA1999-RG6:152 | and the notification shall be in such form as the Authority may determine.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:153 | (5) Upon notification that his application is successful, the applicant shall pay to the
-- src:TA1999-RG6:154 | Authority the fee referred to in regulation 10 (1) (a) and the Authority shall, subject to
-- src:TA1999-RG6:155 | regulation 7, grant a Dealer’s Individual Licence under section 5 of the Act to the
-- src:TA1999-RG6:156 | applicant upon receipt of such payment.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:157 | (6) When granting a Dealer’s Individual Licence, the Authority shall specify the types
-- src:TA1999-RG6:158 | of telecommunication equipment which the holder may manufacture, import, let for hire,
-- src:TA1999-RG6:159 | sell, or offer or possess for sale.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:160 | (7) It shall be a condition of a Dealer’s Individual Licence that the holder of a Dealer’s
-- src:TA1999-RG6:161 | Individual Licence may only sell telecommunication equipment that is not type-approved
-- src:TA1999-RG6:162 | equipment, registered equipment or telecommunication equipment set out in the First
-- src:TA1999-RG6:163 | Schedule —
-- src:TA1999-RG6:164 | (a) to another holder of a Dealer’s Individual Licence; or
-- src:TA1999-RG6:165 | (b) to a person, other than the holder of a Dealer’s Class Licence, for re-export
-- src:TA1999-RG6:166 | and not for use in Singapore.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:167 | (8) A dealer shall obtain a Dealer’s Individual Licence for each of the premises under
-- src:TA1999-RG6:168 | his control or occupation where he manufactures, imports, lets for hire, sells, or offers or
-- src:TA1999-RG6:169 | possesses for sale any telecommunication equipment referred to in paragraph (1).
-- src:TA1999-RG6:170 | (9) The holder of a Dealer’s Individual Licence shall notify the Authority of any change
-- src:TA1999-RG6:171 | in his personal particulars specified in that licence within 14 days of such change.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:172 | (10) A Dealer’s Individual Licence shall be valid for such period as the Authority may
-- src:TA1999-RG6:173 | determine unless revoked or suspended in accordance with the provisions of the Act and
-- src:TA1999-RG6:174 | shall be subject to such conditions as the Authority thinks fit.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:175 | (11) The Authority may add to, vary or waive all or any of, the conditions referred to in
-- src:TA1999-RG6:176 | paragraph (10) and the holder of a Dealer’s Individual Licence shall, at his own expense,
-- src:TA1999-RG6:177 | comply with the varied or additional conditions.
@ref Rg 6 reg 4 (src:TA1999-RG6:140-177)
GIVEN `the dealer wishes to manufacture, import, let for hire, sell, or offer or possess for sale telecommunication equipment that is not type-approved equipment, registered equipment or set out in the First Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 4(1): the dealer must obtain a Dealer's Individual Licence` MEANS
    `the dealer wishes to manufacture, import, let for hire, sell, or offer or possess for sale telecommunication equipment that is not type-approved equipment, registered equipment or set out in the First Schedule`

GIVEN `the application is in the form and manner the Authority determined and supported by the information it required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person furnishes false, misleading or inaccurate information for the purpose of obtaining the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 4(2) and (3): the application is as the regulation requires` MEANS
    `the application is in the form and manner the Authority determined and supported by the information it required` AND (NOT `the person furnishes false, misleading or inaccurate information for the purpose of obtaining the licence`)

GIVEN `the Authority notified the applicant that the application is successful` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant paid the fee referred to in regulation 10(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is not excluded by regulation 7` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 4(4) and (5): the Authority shall grant the Dealer's Individual Licence under section 5 of the Act` MEANS
    `the Authority notified the applicant that the application is successful` AND `the applicant paid the fee referred to in regulation 10(1)(a)` AND `the applicant is not excluded by regulation 7`

GIVEN `the equipment is type-approved equipment, registered equipment or set out in the First Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sale is to another holder of a Dealer's Individual Licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sale is to a person other than the holder of a Dealer's Class Licence, for re-export and not for use in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 4(7): the holder of a Dealer's Individual Licence may sell the equipment` MEANS
    `the equipment is type-approved equipment, registered equipment or set out in the First Schedule`
    OR `the sale is to another holder of a Dealer's Individual Licence`
    OR `the sale is to a person other than the holder of a Dealer's Class Licence, for re-export and not for use in Singapore`

GIVEN `the dealer obtained a Dealer's Individual Licence for each of the premises under its control or occupation where it deals in such equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days after a change in personal particulars specified in the licence, that the holder notified the Authority` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 4(8) and (9): the dealer has done what the regulation requires` MEANS
    `the dealer obtained a Dealer's Individual Licence for each of the premises under its control or occupation where it deals in such equipment`
    AND (`days after a change in personal particulars specified in the licence, that the holder notified the Authority` AT MOST 14)

GIVEN `the Authority specified the types of equipment in the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment is of a type specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 4(6): the holder may deal in the equipment under the licence` MEANS
    `the Authority specified the types of equipment in the licence` AND `the equipment is of a type specified`

GIVEN `the holder complies, at its own expense, with the conditions the Authority thinks fit and any it varied or added` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licence has been revoked or suspended in accordance with the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 4(10) and (11): the Dealer's Individual Licence is valid and its holder is meeting its conditions` MEANS
    `the holder complies, at its own expense, with the conditions the Authority thinks fit and any it varied or added` AND (NOT `the licence has been revoked or suspended in accordance with the Act`)

§ `Rg 6 regulations 5 to 10: class licence of an individual licensee, demonstration, restriction, replacement, renewal, fees`

-- src:TA1999-RG6:180 | 5. —(1) The holder of a Dealer’s Individual Licence who manufactures, imports, lets for
-- src:TA1999-RG6:181 | hire, sells, or offers or possesses for sale any type-approved equipment, registered
-- src:TA1999-RG6:182 | equipment or telecommunication equipment set out in the First Schedule at premises
-- src:TA1999-RG6:183 | other than those in respect of which he has obtained a Dealer’s Individual Licence shall
-- src:TA1999-RG6:184 | be deemed to have been granted a Dealer’s Class Licence in respect of those other
-- src:TA1999-RG6:185 | premises.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:186 | (2) The holder of a Dealer’s Individual Licence who manufactures, imports, lets for hire,
-- src:TA1999-RG6:187 | sells, or offers or possesses for sale any type-approved equipment, registered equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6:188 | or telecommunication equipment set out in the First Schedule at the premises in respect
-- src:TA1999-RG6:189 | of which he has obtained a Dealer’s Individual Licence shall not be deemed to be a
-- src:TA1999-RG6:190 | holder of a Dealer’s Class Licence for such purpose in respect of those premises.
@ref Rg 6 reg 5 (src:TA1999-RG6:180-190)
GIVEN `the holder of a Dealer's Individual Licence deals in type-approved equipment, registered equipment or equipment set out in the First Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the premises are those for which the individual licence was obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 5: the holder is deemed to have been granted a Dealer's Class Licence in respect of the premises` MEANS
    `the holder of a Dealer's Individual Licence deals in type-approved equipment, registered equipment or equipment set out in the First Schedule` AND (NOT `the premises are those for which the individual licence was obtained`)

-- src:TA1999-RG6:193 | 6. —(1) No person shall operate any telecommunication equipment for demonstration
-- src:TA1999-RG6:194 | purposes unless he has obtained the prior approval of the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:195 | (2) It shall be a condition of every licence that a licensee shall not, except with the prior
-- src:TA1999-RG6:196 | approval of the Authority, operate any telecommunication equipment for demonstration
-- src:TA1999-RG6:197 | purposes.
@ref Rg 6 reg 6 (src:TA1999-RG6:193-197)
GIVEN `the Authority gave its prior approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 6: the person may operate the telecommunication equipment for demonstration purposes` MEANS
    `the Authority gave its prior approval`

-- src:TA1999-RG6:200 | 7. No person shall be granted a Dealer’s Individual Licence or be deemed to have been
-- src:TA1999-RG6:201 | granted a Dealer’s Class Licence unless that person is —
-- src:TA1999-RG6:202 | (a) a citizen of Singapore;
-- src:TA1999-RG6:203 | (b) a company incorporated under the Companies Act (Cap. 50);
-- src:TA1999-RG6:204 | (c) a person who carries on a business registered under the Business Registration
-- src:TA1999-RG6:205 | Act (Cap. 32); or
-- src:TA1999-RG6:206 | (d) such other person as the Authority may, in its discretion, consider appropriate
-- src:TA1999-RG6:207 | to hold such licence.
@ref Rg 6 reg 7 (src:TA1999-RG6:200-207)
GIVEN `the person is a citizen of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a company incorporated under the Companies Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person carries on a business registered under the Business Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority considers the person appropriate to hold the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 7: the person may be granted a Dealer's Individual Licence or be deemed granted a Dealer's Class Licence` MEANS
    `the person is a citizen of Singapore` OR `the person is a company incorporated under the Companies Act` OR `the person carries on a business registered under the Business Registration Act` OR `the Authority considers the person appropriate to hold the licence`

-- src:TA1999-RG6:210 | 8. If the Authority is satisfied that any Dealer’s Individual Licence issued by it has been
-- src:TA1999-RG6:211 | lost, destroyed or defaced, the Authority may, upon payment of a fee of $5 by the person
-- src:TA1999-RG6:212 | whose Dealer’s Individual Licence is lost, destroyed or defaced, issue a replacement
-- src:TA1999-RG6:213 | licence to such person.
@ref Rg 6 reg 8 (src:TA1999-RG6:210-213)
GIVEN `the Authority is satisfied the licence was lost, destroyed or defaced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 6 reg 8: the fee in dollars for a replacement Dealer's Individual Licence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the Authority is satisfied the licence was lost, destroyed or defaced` THEN JUST 5 OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:TA1999-RG6:215 | 9. Every application for the renewal of a Dealer’s Individual Licence shall be in such
-- src:TA1999-RG6:216 | form and manner as the Authority may require and accompanied by a renewal fee of
-- src:TA1999-RG6:217 | $250.
@ref Rg 6 reg 9 (src:TA1999-RG6:215-217)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 6 reg 9: the renewal fee in dollars for a Dealer's Individual Licence` MEANS 250

-- src:TA1999-RG6:220 | 10. —(1) The fee payable for a Dealer’s Individual Licence shall be as follows:
-- src:TA1999-RG6:221 | (a) $250 for the first year of that licence; and
-- src:TA1999-RG6:222 | (b) $250 for every subsequent year for the duration of that licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:223 | (2) The fee payable for a Dealer’s Class Licence held by any person who is carrying on
-- src:TA1999-RG6:224 | any business or trade as a dealer shall be $50.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:225 | (3) Payment of fees in respect of a Dealer’s Individual Licence shall be made —
-- src:TA1999-RG6:226 | (a) in respect of a fee referred to in paragraph (1) (a), within 90 days of the
-- src:TA1999-RG6:227 | notification under regulation 4 (4) that the application for a Dealer’s Individual
-- src:TA1999-RG6:228 | Licence is successful; and
-- src:TA1999-RG6:229 | (b) in respect of a fee referred to in paragraph (1) (b), on or before each
-- src:TA1999-RG6:230 | anniversary of the date of issue of the Dealer’s Individual Licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:231 | (4) Payment of fees in respect of a Dealer’s Class Licence shall be made within 90 days
-- src:TA1999-RG6:232 | of the date of the registration under regulation 3 (5).
-- src:TA1999-RG6:233 | (5) If any fee remains unpaid after the date by which such fee should have been paid as
-- src:TA1999-RG6:234 | referred to in paragraph (3) (b) or (4) (b), the following late payment fee shall be charged:
-- src:TA1999-RG6:235 | (a) where the fee is paid after 7 days but before 15 days following the date by
-- src:TA1999-RG6:236 | which such fee should have been paid, $10;
-- src:TA1999-RG6:237 | (b) where the fee is paid after 14 days but before 31 days following the date by
-- src:TA1999-RG6:238 | which such fee should have been paid, $20; and
-- src:TA1999-RG6:239 | (c) where the fee is paid after 30 days following the date by which such fee should
-- src:TA1999-RG6:240 | have been paid, $50.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:241 | (6) It shall be a condition of a licence that the fee referred to in paragraph (1) (b) or (2),
-- src:TA1999-RG6:242 | as the case may be, shall be paid in accordance with this regulation.
@ref Rg 6 reg 10 (src:TA1999-RG6:220-242)
GIVEN `the year of the licence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 6 reg 10(1): the fee for a Dealer's Individual Licence for the year, in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the year of the licence` EQUALS 1 THEN 250 OTHERWISE 250

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 6 reg 10(2): the fee for a Dealer's Class Licence held by a person carrying on a business or trade as a dealer, in dollars` MEANS 50

GIVEN `days after the notification (reg 4(4)) that the application is successful` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 10(3)(a): the first-year fee is paid within time` MEANS
    `days after the notification (reg 4(4)) that the application is successful` AT MOST 90

GIVEN `days after the registration under regulation 3(5)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 10(4): the class licence fee is paid within time` MEANS
    `days after the registration under regulation 3(5)` AT MOST 90

GIVEN `days after the date by which the fee should have been paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 6 reg 10(5): the late payment fee in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `days after the date by which the fee should have been paid` AT MOST 7 THEN 0
           IF `days after the date by which the fee should have been paid` AT MOST 14 THEN 10
           IF `days after the date by which the fee should have been paid` AT MOST 30 THEN 20
           OTHERWISE 50

GIVEN `the fee is paid in accordance with the regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 10(6): the licence condition on fees is met` MEANS
    `the fee is paid in accordance with the regulation`

§ `Rg 6 reg 10(2) and (4), Revised Edition 2004 as printed in the Gazette (1 Jan 2005 to 20 Jul 2005)`

-- The IMDA copy deposited as the "Revised Edition" prints reg 10(2) and (4) as S 478/2005 reg 6 substitutes them (from 21 July 2005), so the two functions
-- above for those paragraphs are the text from 21 July 2005.  The Gazette's Revised Edition 2004 prints them as below (NOTES.md finding 19).
-- src:TA1999-RG6-GAZ-RevEd2004:311 | (2) The fee payable for a Dealer’s Class Licence shall be as follows:
-- src:TA1999-RG6-GAZ-RevEd2004:312 | (a) $50 for the first 5 years from the date of the Authority’s
-- src:TA1999-RG6-GAZ-RevEd2004:313 | acknowledgment under regulation 3 (6); and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-GAZ-RevEd2004:314 | (b) $50 for every subsequent period of 5 years for the duration
-- src:TA1999-RG6-GAZ-RevEd2004:315 | of that licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG6-GAZ-RevEd2004:325 | (4) Payment of fees in respect of a Dealer’s Class Licence shall be
-- src:TA1999-RG6-GAZ-RevEd2004:326 | made —
-- src:TA1999-RG6-GAZ-RevEd2004:327 | (a) in respect of a fee referred to in paragraph (2) (a), within
-- src:TA1999-RG6-GAZ-RevEd2004:328 | 90 days of the date of the registration under regulation 3 (5);
-- src:TA1999-RG6-GAZ-RevEd2004:329 | and
-- src:TA1999-RG6-GAZ-RevEd2004:330 | (b) in respect of a fee referred to in paragraph (2) (b), on or
-- src:TA1999-RG6-GAZ-RevEd2004:331 | before the anniversary of the date of the Authority’s
-- src:TA1999-RG6-GAZ-RevEd2004:332 | acknowledgment under regulation 3 (6) at the end of each
-- src:TA1999-RG6-GAZ-RevEd2004:333 | period of 5 years.
@ref Rg 6 reg 10(2) and (4), Revised Edition 2004 as printed in the Gazette (src:TA1999-RG6-GAZ-RevEd2004:311-315; src:TA1999-RG6-GAZ-RevEd2004:325-333)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 6 reg 10(2) (Revised Edition 2004): the fee for a Dealer's Class Licence for each period of 5 years, in dollars` MEANS 50

GIVEN `days after the registration under regulation 3(5)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 10(4)(a) (Revised Edition 2004): the first-period class licence fee is paid within time` MEANS
    `days after the registration under regulation 3(5)` AT MOST 90

GIVEN `the payment is made on or before the anniversary of the date of the Authority's acknowledgment under regulation 3(6) at the end of the period of 5 years` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 10(4)(b) (Revised Edition 2004): the fee for a subsequent period of 5 years is paid within time` MEANS
    `the payment is made on or before the anniversary of the date of the Authority's acknowledgment under regulation 3(6) at the end of the period of 5 years`

-- Which form governs: the Revised Edition 2004 from 1 Jan 2005 (the first day this encoding speaks for, NOTES.md Fork B), S 478/2005's from 21 Jul 2005.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 10(2) and (4): the class licence fee falls due for each period of 5 years, on the date` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 1 2005) THEN NOTHING
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§ `Rg 6 regulations 11 to 17: conduct of dealers, inspection`

-- src:TA1999-RG6:248 | 11. It shall be a condition of a licence that the licensee shall not manufacture, import, let
-- src:TA1999-RG6:249 | for hire, sell, or offer or possess for sale any telecommunication equipment set out in the
-- src:TA1999-RG6:250 | Third Schedule except where approved by the Authority and in accordance with such
-- src:TA1999-RG6:251 | terms and conditions as the Authority may impose.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:252 | Equipment to be used for lawful purpose, safe manner, etc.
@ref Rg 6 reg 11 (src:TA1999-RG6:248-252)
GIVEN `the equipment is set out in the Third Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority approved it, and the licensee complies with the terms and conditions the Authority imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 11: the licensee may manufacture, import, let for hire, sell, or offer or possess for sale the equipment` MEANS
    (NOT `the equipment is set out in the Third Schedule`) OR `the Authority approved it, and the licensee complies with the terms and conditions the Authority imposed`

-- src:TA1999-RG6:253 | 12. A licensee shall ensure that any telecommunication equipment in his possession is
-- src:TA1999-RG6:254 | not used for any unlawful purpose and shall operate it in a manner which is safe and
-- src:TA1999-RG6:255 | which does not impair or interfere with the efficient and convenient working or
-- src:TA1999-RG6:256 | maintenance of any other telecommunication system or service authorised by the
-- src:TA1999-RG6:257 | Authority.
@ref Rg 6 reg 12 (src:TA1999-RG6:253-257)
GIVEN `the equipment is used for an unlawful purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment is operated in a manner that is not safe or that impairs or interferes with another authorised telecommunication system or service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 12: the licensee has breached the regulation` MEANS
    `the equipment is used for an unlawful purpose` OR `the equipment is operated in a manner that is not safe or that impairs or interferes with another authorised telecommunication system or service`

-- src:TA1999-RG6:260 | 13. —(1) Except as otherwise provided in these Regulations or by the terms and
-- src:TA1999-RG6:261 | conditions of a licence, every dealer having access to any telecommunication —
-- src:TA1999-RG6:262 | (a) shall hold strictly secret all such telecommunication, other than a
-- src:TA1999-RG6:263 | telecommunication transmitted or sent for general information;
-- src:TA1999-RG6:264 | (b) shall not, directly or indirectly, disclose the contents of the telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG6:265 | except —
-- src:TA1999-RG6:266 | (i) to a person entitled to become acquainted with the telecommunication;
-- src:TA1999-RG6:267 | or
-- src:TA1999-RG6:268 | (ii) to an authorised officer,
-- src:TA1999-RG6:269 | or except where the disclosure is otherwise authorised or required by law; and
-- src:TA1999-RG6:270 | (c) shall not make any use of such telecommunication.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:271 | (2) No dealer having access to any telecommunication shall print or publish or cause to
-- src:TA1999-RG6:272 | be printed or published in any newspaper, pamphlet, book or other document, that
-- src:TA1999-RG6:273 | telecommunication, whether such telecommunication is for private or general reception.
@ref Rg 6 reg 13 (src:TA1999-RG6:260-273)
GIVEN `the telecommunication was transmitted or sent for general information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dealer discloses the contents to a person entitled to them or to an authorised officer, or the law authorises or requires the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dealer discloses the contents otherwise, or makes any use of the telecommunication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 13(1): the dealer has breached the duty of secrecy` MEANS
    (NOT `the telecommunication was transmitted or sent for general information`) AND `the dealer discloses the contents otherwise, or makes any use of the telecommunication` AND (NOT `the dealer discloses the contents to a person entitled to them or to an authorised officer, or the law authorises or requires the disclosure`)

GIVEN `the dealer prints or publishes, or causes to be printed or published, the telecommunication in a newspaper, pamphlet, book or other document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 13(2): the dealer has breached the prohibition on publishing` MEANS
    `the dealer prints or publishes, or causes to be printed or published, the telecommunication in a newspaper, pamphlet, book or other document`

-- src:TA1999-RG6:276 | 14. —(1) No dealer shall transmit or permit the transmission of superfluous signals.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:277 | (2) No person shall test any transmission, or allow or conduct any trial or practical
-- src:TA1999-RG6:278 | transmission, except in such circumstances as to preclude the possibility of interference
-- src:TA1999-RG6:279 | with any other telecommunication.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:280 | (3) No person shall conduct any test transmission other than on dummy load without the
-- src:TA1999-RG6:281 | prior approval of the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:282 | (4) No dealer shall transmit or permit the transmission of —
-- src:TA1999-RG6:283 | (a) any message containing indecent, obscene or offensive language;
-- src:TA1999-RG6:284 | (b) any message for an illegal purpose;
-- src:TA1999-RG6:285 | (c) any message which interferes with the operation of any type-approved
-- src:TA1999-RG6:286 | equipment, registered equipment or telecommunication equipment set out in the
-- src:TA1999-RG6:287 | First Schedule; or
-- src:TA1999-RG6:288 | (d) any message which to his knowledge is false or misleading and likely to
-- src:TA1999-RG6:289 | prejudice the efficiency of any emergency service or endanger the safety of any
-- src:TA1999-RG6:290 | person, place, premises, vessel, aircraft or vehicle.
@ref Rg 6 reg 14 (src:TA1999-RG6:276-290)
GIVEN `the dealer transmits or permits the transmission of superfluous signals` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 14(1): the dealer has breached the regulation` MEANS
    `the dealer transmits or permits the transmission of superfluous signals`

GIVEN `the test or trial transmission can cause interference with other telecommunication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the test transmission is on dummy load` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority gave its prior approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 14(2) and (3): the test transmission is permitted` MEANS
    (NOT `the test or trial transmission can cause interference with other telecommunication`) AND (`the test transmission is on dummy load` OR `the Authority gave its prior approval`)

GIVEN `the message contains indecent, obscene or offensive language` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the message is for an illegal purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the message interferes with the operation of type-approved equipment, registered equipment or equipment set out in the First Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the message is, to the dealer's knowledge, false or misleading and likely to prejudice the efficiency of any emergency service or endanger safety` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 14(4): the dealer may transmit or permit the transmission of the message` MEANS
        (NOT `the message contains indecent, obscene or offensive language`)
    AND (NOT `the message is for an illegal purpose`)
    AND (NOT `the message interferes with the operation of type-approved equipment, registered equipment or equipment set out in the First Schedule`)
    AND (NOT `the message is, to the dealer's knowledge, false or misleading and likely to prejudice the efficiency of any emergency service or endanger safety`)

-- src:TA1999-RG6:296 | 15. —(1) The holder of a Dealer’s Individual Licence shall permit an authorised officer
-- src:TA1999-RG6:297 | or a police officer not below the rank of sergeant, upon production of proof of identity, to
-- src:TA1999-RG6:298 | inspect his licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:299 | (2) Where his licence is not immediately available, the holder of a Dealer’s Individual
-- src:TA1999-RG6:300 | Licence shall produce his licence at the office of the Authority or a police station named
-- src:TA1999-RG6:301 | by the police officer within a reasonable period.
@ref Rg 6 reg 15 (src:TA1999-RG6:296-301)
GIVEN `the holder permits an authorised officer or a police officer not below the rank of sergeant, on production of proof of identity, to inspect the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `if the licence is not immediately available, the holder produces it within a reasonable period at the Authority's office or the police station named` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 15: the holder has done what the regulation requires` MEANS
    `the holder permits an authorised officer or a police officer not below the rank of sergeant, on production of proof of identity, to inspect the licence` AND `if the licence is not immediately available, the holder produces it within a reasonable period at the Authority's office or the police station named`

-- src:TA1999-RG6:304 | 16. —(1) The Authority may appoint authorised officers as inspection officers for the
-- src:TA1999-RG6:305 | inspection and examination of any equipment approved under these Regulations, any
-- src:TA1999-RG6:306 | premises owned or occupied by a dealer where he manufactures, imports, lets for hire,
-- src:TA1999-RG6:307 | sells, or offers or possesses for sale any telecommunication equipment, and any
-- src:TA1999-RG6:308 | telecommunication equipment found therein.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:309 | (2) For the purpose of ensuring that the Act, these Regulations and any condition of a
-- src:TA1999-RG6:310 | licence are complied with, an inspection officer shall be entitled, at any time and upon
-- src:TA1999-RG6:311 | production of proof of identity, to enter any land, building, vessel, aircraft or vehicle
-- src:TA1999-RG6:312 | where any telecommunication equipment is kept or stored and to inspect, examine or test
-- src:TA1999-RG6:313 | such equipment.
@ref Rg 6 reg 16 (src:TA1999-RG6:304-313)
GIVEN `the person is an authorised officer appointed by the Authority as an inspection officer, on production of proof of identity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 16: the inspection officer may enter the place where telecommunication equipment is kept or stored and inspect, examine or test it` MEANS
    `the person is an authorised officer appointed by the Authority as an inspection officer, on production of proof of identity`

-- src:TA1999-RG6:316 | 17. No person shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG6:317 | (a) refuse entry to an authorised officer to any land, building, vessel, aircraft or
-- src:TA1999-RG6:318 | vehicle to inspect, examine or test any telecommunication equipment contained or
-- src:TA1999-RG6:319 | stored therein; or
-- src:TA1999-RG6:320 | (b) in any way obstruct or hinder an authorised officer in the execution of a duty
-- src:TA1999-RG6:321 | imposed or power conferred upon that officer by the Act, these Regulations or any
-- src:TA1999-RG6:322 | other written law.
@ref Rg 6 reg 17 (src:TA1999-RG6:316-322)
GIVEN `the person refuses entry to an authorised officer to inspect, examine or test the telecommunication equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person obstructs or hinders an authorised officer in the execution of a duty or power under the Act, these Regulations or any other written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 17: the person has breached the regulation` MEANS
    `the person refuses entry to an authorised officer to inspect, examine or test the telecommunication equipment` OR `the person obstructs or hinders an authorised officer in the execution of a duty or power under the Act, these Regulations or any other written law`

§ `Rg 6 regulations 18 to 21: importation, production, type-approval (2004 form), registration (2004 form)`

-- src:TA1999-RG6:329 | 18. —(1) No person shall import any telecommunication equipment without the prior
-- src:TA1999-RG6:330 | approval of the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:331 | (2) A person applying for approval under paragraph (1) shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG6:332 | (a) furnish such particulars as may be required by the Authority; and
-- src:TA1999-RG6:333 | (b) obtain a permit under the Regulation of Imports and Exports Regulations
-- src:TA1999-RG6:334 | (Cap. 272A, Rg 1) for the equipment before such equipment is imported.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:335 | (3) No person shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG6:336 | (a) furnish any false or misleading information to the Authority for the purpose of
-- src:TA1999-RG6:337 | obtaining the approval of the Authority under paragraph (1); or
-- src:TA1999-RG6:338 | (b) falsify or fabricate any decision that the Authority may make upon the
-- src:TA1999-RG6:339 | application for approval under paragraph (1).
-- src:TA1999-RG6:340 | (4) Where any person contravenes paragraph (3), any approval issued to that person
-- src:TA1999-RG6:341 | under this regulation shall be null and void.
@ref Rg 6 reg 18 (src:TA1999-RG6:329-341)
GIVEN `the Authority gave its prior approval to the importation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 18(1): the person may import the telecommunication equipment` MEANS
    `the Authority gave its prior approval to the importation`

GIVEN `the applicant furnished the particulars the Authority required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant obtained a permit under the Regulation of Imports and Exports Regulations before the equipment is imported` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 18(2): the application for approval to import is as the regulation requires` MEANS
    `the applicant furnished the particulars the Authority required` AND `the applicant obtained a permit under the Regulation of Imports and Exports Regulations before the equipment is imported`

GIVEN `the person furnishes false or misleading information to the Authority for the purpose of obtaining the approval, or falsifies or fabricates a decision of the Authority on the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 18(3) and (4): the person has breached the regulation, and any approval issued to the person is null and void` MEANS
    `the person furnishes false or misleading information to the Authority for the purpose of obtaining the approval, or falsifies or fabricates a decision of the Authority on the application`

-- src:TA1999-RG6:344 | 19. The Authority may direct a person who imports any telecommunication equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6:345 | to produce it for testing or inspection by the Authority and that person shall comply with
-- src:TA1999-RG6:346 | such direction at his own expense.
@ref Rg 6 reg 19 (src:TA1999-RG6:344-346)
GIVEN `the Authority directed the person who imports telecommunication equipment to produce it for testing or inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 19: the person must produce the equipment at the person's own expense` MEANS
    `the Authority directed the person who imports telecommunication equipment to produce it for testing or inspection`

-- src:TA1999-RG6:349 | 20. —(1) Subject to paragraph (2) and regulation 4 (7), it shall be a condition of a
-- src:TA1999-RG6:350 | licence that the licensee shall not sell —
-- src:TA1999-RG6:351 | (a) any type of telecommunication equipment to be used for connection to any
-- src:TA1999-RG6:352 | telecommunication system or equipment belonging to a telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG6:353 | system licensee; or
-- src:TA1999-RG6:354 | (b) any type of radio-communication equipment to be used in Singapore,
-- src:TA1999-RG6:355 | unless the type of equipment has been approved by the Authority to be sold.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:356 | (2) No approval for sale under paragraph (1) is required in respect of any registered
-- src:TA1999-RG6:357 | equipment or any telecommunication equipment set out in the First Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:358 | (3) An application for type-approval of any equipment referred to in paragraph (1) shall
-- src:TA1999-RG6:359 | be made to the Authority in such manner as the Authority may determine.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:360 | (4) No dealer shall furnish any false or misleading information to the Authority for the
-- src:TA1999-RG6:361 | purpose of obtaining any approval under paragraph (1).
-- src:TA1999-RG6:362 | (5) Where any dealer contravenes paragraph (4), any approval issued to that dealer
-- src:TA1999-RG6:363 | under this regulation shall be null and void.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:364 | (6) The fee for an application for approval under paragraph (1) is specified in the Fourth
-- src:TA1999-RG6:365 | Schedule.
@ref Rg 6 reg 20 (src:TA1999-RG6:349-365)
GIVEN `the equipment is to be used for connection to a telecommunication system or equipment belonging to a telecommunication system licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment is radio-communication equipment to be used in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equipment is registered equipment or set out in the First Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the type of equipment has been approved by the Authority to be sold` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee sells it under a Dealer's Individual Licence under regulation 4(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 20(1) and (2) (2004 Revised Edition): the licensee may sell the equipment` MEANS
    (NOT (`the equipment is to be used for connection to a telecommunication system or equipment belonging to a telecommunication system licensee` OR `the equipment is radio-communication equipment to be used in Singapore`))
    OR `the equipment is registered equipment or set out in the First Schedule`
    OR `the type of equipment has been approved by the Authority to be sold`
    OR `the licensee sells it under a Dealer's Individual Licence under regulation 4(7)`

GIVEN `the dealer furnishes false or misleading information to the Authority for the purpose of obtaining the approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 20(4) and (5): the dealer has breached the regulation, and the approval is null and void` MEANS
    `the dealer furnishes false or misleading information to the Authority for the purpose of obtaining the approval`

GIVEN `the application for type-approval is made to the Authority in the manner it determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fee in the Fourth Schedule is paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 20(3) and (6): the application for type-approval is as the regulation requires` MEANS
    `the application for type-approval is made to the Authority in the manner it determined` AND `the fee in the Fourth Schedule is paid`

-- src:TA1999-RG6:368 | 21. —(1) Upon an application in such form as the Authority may determine, the
-- src:TA1999-RG6:369 | Authority may register for sale any telecommunication equipment which has been
-- src:TA1999-RG6:370 | certified or tested by such body as the Authority may determine.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:371 | (2) The registration under paragraph (1) shall be valid for 5 years and upon an
-- src:TA1999-RG6:372 | application for renewal in such form as the Authority may determine, may be renewed for
-- src:TA1999-RG6:373 | periods not exceeding 5 years at a time.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:374 | (3) The fee payable for registration shall be $100 for the first 5 years and $50 for every
-- src:TA1999-RG6:375 | renewed period of 5 years or less.
@ref Rg 6 reg 21 (src:TA1999-RG6:368-375)
GIVEN `the equipment has been certified or tested by a body the Authority determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is in the form the Authority determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 21(1) (2004 Revised Edition): the Authority may register the equipment for sale` MEANS
    `the equipment has been certified or tested by a body the Authority determined` AND `the application is in the form the Authority determined`

GIVEN `years since the registration or last renewal` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 21(2) (2004 Revised Edition): the registration is still valid` MEANS
    `years since the registration or last renewal` LESS THAN 5

GIVEN `this is the first registration period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 6 reg 21(3) (2004 Revised Edition): the fee payable for registration in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `this is the first registration period` THEN 100 OTHERWISE 50

§ `Rg 6 regulations 23 to 25: disposal, offence, waiver`

-- src:TA1999-RG6:394 | 23. Where any person —
-- src:TA1999-RG6:395 | (a) imports any telecommunication equipment without the approval of the
-- src:TA1999-RG6:396 | Authority; or
-- src:TA1999-RG6:397 | (b) manufactures, lets for hire, sells, or offers or possesses for sale any
-- src:TA1999-RG6:398 | telecommunication equipment which does not meet the standards or specifications
-- src:TA1999-RG6:399 | published by the Authority from time to time,
-- src:TA1999-RG6:400 | the Authority may direct that person to dispose of the equipment in any manner which the
-- src:TA1999-RG6:401 | Authority thinks fit and that person shall comply with such direction at his own expense.
@ref Rg 6 reg 23 (src:TA1999-RG6:394-401)
GIVEN `the person imports telecommunication equipment without the Authority's approval` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person manufactures, lets for hire, sells, or offers or possesses for sale equipment that does not meet the standards or specifications the Authority published` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 23: the Authority may direct the person to dispose of the equipment as it thinks fit, at the person's own expense` MEANS
    `the person imports telecommunication equipment without the Authority's approval` OR `the person manufactures, lets for hire, sells, or offers or possesses for sale equipment that does not meet the standards or specifications the Authority published`

-- src:TA1999-RG6:404 | 24. Any person who contravenes regulation 3 (5), (7), (8), (9) or (10), 4 (3), (8) or (9), 6
-- src:TA1999-RG6:405 | (1), 12, 13, 14, 15, 17, 18 (1), (2) or (3), 19, 20 (4) or 23 shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref Rg 6 reg 24 (src:TA1999-RG6:404-405)
GIVEN `regulation` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 24 (2004 Revised Edition): breach of this regulation is an offence` MEANS
    elem `regulation` (LIST "3(5)", "3(7)", "3(8)", "3(9)", "3(10)", "4(3)", "4(8)", "4(9)", "6(1)", "12", "13", "14", "15", "17", "18(1)", "18(2)", "18(3)", "19", "20(4)", "23")

-- src:TA1999-RG6:408 | 25. —(1) The Minister, or the Authority with the approval of the Minister, may —
-- src:TA1999-RG6:409 | (a) waive any or all fees payable under these Regulations; or
-- src:TA1999-RG6:410 | (b) exempt any person from any or all provisions of these Regulations.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:411 | (2) A waiver or an exemption granted under paragraph (1) may be notified in writing to
-- src:TA1999-RG6:412 | the person concerned, and need not be published in the Gazette.
@ref Rg 6 reg 25 (src:TA1999-RG6:408-412)
GIVEN `the Minister, or the Authority with the Minister's approval, waives the fees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister, or the Authority with the Minister's approval, exempts the person from the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 reg 25: the fees or the provision do not apply to the person` MEANS
    `the Minister, or the Authority with the Minister's approval, waives the fees` OR `the Minister, or the Authority with the Minister's approval, exempts the person from the provision`

§ `Rg 6 Schedules`

-- src:TA1999-RG6:413 | FIRST SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-RG6:414 | Regulations 3 (1), (5) and (11),
-- src:TA1999-RG6:415 | 4 (1) and (7), 5, 14 (4) and
-- src:TA1999-RG6:416 | 20 (2) and paragraphs 1
-- src:TA1999-RG6:417 | and 2 of Second Schedule
-- src:TA1999-RG6:419 | TELECOMMUNICATION EQUIPMENT
-- src:TA1999-RG6:420 | NOT REQUIRING APPROVAL
-- src:TA1999-RG6:422 | 1. Telephone (Standard/Multi-Feature/Image/Data/Switching)
-- src:TA1999-RG6:423 | 2. Telephone Line Interface
-- src:TA1999-RG6:424 | 3. Telephone Ancillary
-- src:TA1999-RG6:425 | 4. Autodialler
-- src:TA1999-RG6:426 | 5. Auto Answering/Recording Set
-- src:TA1999-RG6:427 | 6. Caller Identification Equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6:428 | 7. Security Alarm System
-- src:TA1999-RG6:429 | 8. Facsimile Transceiver
-- src:TA1999-RG6:430 | 9. Voice Band Modem
-- src:TA1999-RG6:431 | 10. EFTPOS/CCAT
-- src:TA1999-RG6:432 | 11. Telex Equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6:433 | 12. Digital Leased Circuit Equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6:434 | 13. Other equipment as determined by the Authority.
@ref Rg 6 First Schedule (src:TA1999-RG6:413-434)
GIVEN `equipment` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 First Schedule (2004 Revised Edition): this is telecommunication equipment not requiring approval` MEANS
    elem equipment (LIST "Telephone (Standard/Multi-Feature/Image/Data/Switching)", "Telephone Line Interface", "Telephone Ancillary", "Autodialler"
                        , "Auto Answering/Recording Set", "Caller Identification Equipment", "Security Alarm System", "Facsimile Transceiver"
                        , "Voice Band Modem", "EFTPOS/CCAT", "Telex Equipment", "Digital Leased Circuit Equipment", "Other equipment as determined by the Authority")

-- src:TA1999-RG6:436 | SECOND SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-RG6:437 | Regulation 3 (2)
-- src:TA1999-RG6:439 | CONDITIONS OF DEALER’S CLASS LICENCE
-- src:TA1999-RG6:441 | 1. The holder of a Dealer’s Class Licence (referred to in this Schedule as the Class
-- src:TA1999-RG6:442 | Licensee) shall manufacture, import, let for hire, sell, or offer or possess for sale only —
-- src:TA1999-RG6:443 | (a) telecommunication equipment approved for sale under regulation 20 (1);
-- src:TA1999-RG6:444 | (b) telecommunication equipment registered for sale under regulation 21 (1); or
-- src:TA1999-RG6:445 | (c) telecommunication equipment set out in the First Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:446 | 2. A Class Licensee who wishes to sell any registered equipment or telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG6:447 | equipment set out in the First Schedule shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG6:448 | (a) before selling such telecommunication equipment, ensure that it meets the
-- src:TA1999-RG6:449 | standards and specifications for the sale of such telecommunication equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6:450 | published by the Authority in the manner it thinks fit;
-- src:TA1999-RG6:451 | (b) ensure that it works correctly with the relevant telecommunication system or
-- src:TA1999-RG6:452 | equipment of the telecommunication system licensee to which it is connected; and
-- src:TA1999-RG6:453 | (c) cease to sell the telecommunication equipment if so directed by the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG6:454 | and dispose of the telecommunication equipment at his own expense in the
-- src:TA1999-RG6:455 | manner directed by the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:456 | 3. A Class Licensee shall, if required by the Authority, produce any telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG6:457 | equipment for testing or inspection by the Authority and all expenses incurred in
-- src:TA1999-RG6:458 | connection with the testing or inspection shall be borne by the Class Licensee.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:459 | 4. A Class Licensee shall not have in his possession for sale any device or equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6:460 | which is capable of monitoring or intercepting the transmission of a radio-communication
-- src:TA1999-RG6:461 | network.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:462 | 5. —(1) A Class Licensee shall not have in his possession for sale, hire or use any
-- src:TA1999-RG6:463 | device or equipment which can be used —
-- src:TA1999-RG6:464 | (a) to alter, delete or remove any identification code or number of any
-- src:TA1999-RG6:465 | telecommunication equipment which can be used to obtain any
-- src:TA1999-RG6:466 | telecommunication services from telecommunication licensees; or
-- src:TA1999-RG6:467 | (b) to insert or duplicate any identification code or number of such
-- src:TA1999-RG6:468 | telecommunication equipment in any other telecommunication equipment.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:469 | (2) For the purposes of this paragraph, telecommunication equipment includes
-- src:TA1999-RG6:470 | subscriber identification module (“SIM”) cards.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:471 | 6. —(1) A Class Licensee who imports any telecommunication equipment into
-- src:TA1999-RG6:472 | Singapore for the purpose of re-export —
-- src:TA1999-RG6:473 | (a) shall, unless the Authority otherwise directs, immediately move the
-- src:TA1999-RG6:474 | telecommunication equipment into a free trade zone under the Free Trade Zones
-- src:TA1999-RG6:475 | Act (Cap. 114) and keep it there pending re-export;
-- src:TA1999-RG6:476 | (b) shall not sell it to any person for use in Singapore; and
-- src:TA1999-RG6:477 | (c) shall re-export the telecommunication equipment and furnish satisfactory
-- src:TA1999-RG6:478 | evidence of the re-export to the Authority within such time as may be stipulated
-- src:TA1999-RG6:479 | by the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:480 | (2) A Class Licensee shall, if required by the Authority, give a written undertaking that
-- src:TA1999-RG6:481 | the telecommunication equipment declared to be for export purposes will not be sold, or
-- src:TA1999-RG6:482 | offered or possessed for sale in Singapore.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:483 | 7. A Class Licensee shall not manufacture, let for hire, sell, or offer or possess for sale
-- src:TA1999-RG6:484 | any telecommunication equipment set out in the Third Schedule or any
-- src:TA1999-RG6:485 | telecommunication equipment which does not meet the standards or specifications
-- src:TA1999-RG6:486 | published by the Authority from time to time.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:487 | 8. A Class Licensee shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG6:488 | (a) affix or ensure that there is affixed, on all type-approved equipment intended
-- src:TA1999-RG6:489 | for use in Singapore, labels stating or indicating that the telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG6:490 | equipment is type-approved before such telecommunication equipment is
-- src:TA1999-RG6:491 | displayed or offered for sale;
-- src:TA1999-RG6:492 | (b) affix or ensure that there is affixed such other labels as the Authority considers
-- src:TA1999-RG6:493 | necessary on any telecommunication equipment before such telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG6:494 | equipment is displayed or offered for sale;
-- src:TA1999-RG6:495 | (c) ensure that every advertisement, pamphlet or brochure relating to any
-- src:TA1999-RG6:496 | telecommunication equipment which he sells or offers for sale contains such
-- src:TA1999-RG6:497 | information as the Authority may specify;
-- src:TA1999-RG6:498 | (d) refrain from affixing, on any telecommunication equipment which is not type-
-- src:TA1999-RG6:499 | approved equipment, any label stating or indicating that the telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG6:500 | equipment is type-approved; and
-- src:TA1999-RG6:501 | (e) comply with such other labelling requirements as may be published by the
-- src:TA1999-RG6:502 | Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:503 | 9. A Class Licensee shall inform every purchaser or hirer to whom he sells or lets for
-- src:TA1999-RG6:504 | hire any telecommunication equipment of the need to obtain a licence from the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG6:505 | under the Act and these Regulations for the possession, operation, installation or use of
-- src:TA1999-RG6:506 | that telecommunication equipment.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:507 | 10. Except with the Authority’s prior written consent, a Class Licensee shall not assign,
-- src:TA1999-RG6:508 | transfer, sublet or otherwise dispose of any benefit of his Dealer’s Class Licence, or
-- src:TA1999-RG6:509 | permit any person to participate in any benefit or authority granted by his licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:510 | 11. In addition to the conditions of the Dealer’s Class Licence, a Class Licensee shall
-- src:TA1999-RG6:511 | comply with the provisions of the Act, these Regulations and any code of practice issued
-- src:TA1999-RG6:512 | under the Act.
@ref Rg 6 Second Schedule (src:TA1999-RG6:436-512)
GIVEN `the licensee manufactures, imports, lets for hire, sells, or offers or possesses for sale only approved, registered or First Schedule equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee, before selling registered or First Schedule equipment, ensured it meets the Authority's published standards and works correctly with the licensee's system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee ceases to sell and disposes of the equipment as the Authority directs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 Second Schedule items 1 and 2: the Class Licensee is meeting the conditions on what it may deal in` MEANS
    `the licensee manufactures, imports, lets for hire, sells, or offers or possesses for sale only approved, registered or First Schedule equipment`
    AND `the licensee, before selling registered or First Schedule equipment, ensured it meets the Authority's published standards and works correctly with the licensee's system`
    AND `the licensee ceases to sell and disposes of the equipment as the Authority directs`

GIVEN `the Class Licensee produces equipment for testing or inspection when the Authority requires, and bears the expenses` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 Second Schedule item 3: the Class Licensee is meeting the condition` MEANS
    `the Class Licensee produces equipment for testing or inspection when the Authority requires, and bears the expenses`

GIVEN `the Class Licensee has in its possession for sale a device capable of monitoring or intercepting the transmission of a radio-communication network` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 Second Schedule item 4: the Class Licensee is meeting the condition` MEANS
    (NOT `the Class Licensee has in its possession for sale a device capable of monitoring or intercepting the transmission of a radio-communication network`)

GIVEN `the Class Licensee has in its possession for sale, hire or use a device that can alter, delete or remove, or insert or duplicate, an identification code or number of telecommunication equipment (including a SIM card)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 Second Schedule item 5: the Class Licensee is meeting the condition` MEANS
    (NOT `the Class Licensee has in its possession for sale, hire or use a device that can alter, delete or remove, or insert or duplicate, an identification code or number of telecommunication equipment (including a SIM card)`)

GIVEN `the Class Licensee moved equipment imported for re-export into a free trade zone and kept it there pending re-export, unless the Authority otherwise directed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Class Licensee sells it to any person for use in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Class Licensee re-exports it and furnishes satisfactory evidence within the time the Authority stipulated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Class Licensee gave the written undertaking the Authority required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 Second Schedule item 6: the Class Licensee is meeting the condition on imports for re-export` MEANS
        `the Class Licensee moved equipment imported for re-export into a free trade zone and kept it there pending re-export, unless the Authority otherwise directed`
    AND (NOT `the Class Licensee sells it to any person for use in Singapore`)
    AND `the Class Licensee re-exports it and furnishes satisfactory evidence within the time the Authority stipulated`
    AND `the Class Licensee gave the written undertaking the Authority required`

GIVEN `the equipment is set out in the Third Schedule or does not meet the standards or specifications the Authority published` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 Second Schedule item 7: the Class Licensee may manufacture, let for hire, sell, or offer or possess for sale the equipment` MEANS
    (NOT `the equipment is set out in the Third Schedule or does not meet the standards or specifications the Authority published`)

GIVEN `the Class Licensee affixed the labels the Authority specified, and its advertisements, pamphlets and brochures contain the information the Authority specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Class Licensee affixed a label stating that equipment which is not type-approved is type-approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 Second Schedule item 8: the Class Licensee is meeting the labelling conditions` MEANS
    `the Class Licensee affixed the labels the Authority specified, and its advertisements, pamphlets and brochures contain the information the Authority specified` AND (NOT `the Class Licensee affixed a label stating that equipment which is not type-approved is type-approved`)

GIVEN `the Class Licensee informed every purchaser or hirer of the need to obtain a licence from the Authority under the Act and these Regulations for the possession, operation, installation or use of the equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 Second Schedule item 9: the Class Licensee is meeting the condition` MEANS
    `the Class Licensee informed every purchaser or hirer of the need to obtain a licence from the Authority under the Act and these Regulations for the possession, operation, installation or use of the equipment`

GIVEN `the Class Licensee has the Authority's prior written consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Class Licensee assigns, transfers, sublets or otherwise disposes of any benefit of the licence, or permits another to participate in any benefit or authority granted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 Second Schedule item 10: the Class Licensee may do it` MEANS
    `the Class Licensee has the Authority's prior written consent` OR (NOT `the Class Licensee assigns, transfers, sublets or otherwise disposes of any benefit of the licence, or permits another to participate in any benefit or authority granted`)

GIVEN `the Class Licensee complies with the provisions of the Act, these Regulations and any code of practice issued under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 Second Schedule item 11: the Class Licensee is meeting the condition` MEANS
    `the Class Licensee complies with the provisions of the Act, these Regulations and any code of practice issued under the Act`

-- src:TA1999-RG6:514 | THIRD SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-RG6:515 | Regulation 11 and paragraph 7
-- src:TA1999-RG6:516 | of the Second Schedule
-- src:TA1999-RG6:518 | PROHIBITED TELECOMMUNICATION EQUIPMENT
-- src:TA1999-RG6:520 | 1. Scanning Receivers
-- src:TA1999-RG6:521 | 2. Military Communication Equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6:522 | 3. Telephone Voice Changing Equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6:523 | 4. Automatic Call Diverters
-- src:TA1999-RG6:524 | 5. Radio-communication Equipment operating in frequency bands 890-915 MHz and
-- src:TA1999-RG6:525 | 935-960 MHz except Cellular Mobile Phones or such other equipment approved by the
-- src:TA1999-RG6:526 | Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG6:527 | 6. Radio-communication Jamming Devices operating in any frequency band.
@ref Rg 6 Third Schedule (src:TA1999-RG6:514-527)
GIVEN `equipment` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 6 Third Schedule (2004 Revised Edition): this is prohibited telecommunication equipment` MEANS
    elem equipment (LIST "Scanning Receivers", "Military Communication Equipment", "Telephone Voice Changing Equipment", "Automatic Call Diverters"
                        , "Radio-communication Equipment operating in frequency bands 890-915 MHz and 935-960 MHz except Cellular Mobile Phones or such other equipment approved by the Authority"
                        , "Radio-communication Jamming Devices operating in any frequency band")

-- src:TA1999-RG6:528 | FOURTH SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-RG6:529 | Regulation 20 (6)
-- src:TA1999-RG6:531 | FEES FOR APPLICATION BY DEALERS FOR APPROVAL OF
-- src:TA1999-RG6:532 | TELECOMMUNICATION EQUIPMENT
-- src:TA1999-RG6:534 | First column Second column Third column
-- src:TA1999-RG6:535 | Type of telecommunication equipment Application fee Modification or
-- src:TA1999-RG6:536 | re-test fee
-- src:TA1999-RG6:537 | LINE-BASED EQUIPMENT
-- src:TA1999-RG6:538 | 1. Call Switching System/Multiplex System $1,200 $600
-- src:TA1999-RG6:539 | (a) ATM UNI Equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6:540 | (b) PABX
-- src:TA1999-RG6:541 | (c) Key Telephone System
-- src:TA1999-RG6:542 | (d) Multi-Line System
-- src:TA1999-RG6:543 | (e) Voice Messaging System
-- src:TA1999-RG6:544 | (f) ISDN Equipment (Primary Rate)
-- src:TA1999-RG6:545 | (g) ISDN Equipment (Basic Rate with built-in
-- src:TA1999-RG6:546 | NT-1)
-- src:TA1999-RG6:547 | 2. Complex Terminal Equipment $900 $450
-- src:TA1999-RG6:548 | (a) ISDN Equipment (Basic Rate)
-- src:TA1999-RG6:549 | (b) ISDN Equipment (Standalone NT-1)
-- src:TA1999-RG6:550 | (c) Coinphone/Payphone
-- src:TA1999-RG6:551 | 3. Single Line Terminal Equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6:552 | (a) Telephone/Telephone Line Interface/ $700 $350
-- src:TA1999-RG6:553 | Telephone Ancillary/ Autodialler/Auto
-- src:TA1999-RG6:554 | Answering Set/Security Alarm
-- src:TA1999-RG6:555 | System/Modem/EFTPOS/CCAT
-- src:TA1999-RG6:556 | (b) Caller Identification Device/Fax $900 $450
-- src:TA1999-RG6:557 | Transceiver/Fax Modem/Telex
-- src:TA1999-RG6:558 | Equipment/Digital Leased Circuit Equipment
-- src:TA1999-RG6:561 | RADIO-COMMUNICATION EQUIPMENT
-- src:TA1999-RG6:562 | 1. Analogue Radio-communication Equipment $2,000 $1,000
-- src:TA1999-RG6:563 | (a) VHF/UHF Mobile Transceiver
-- src:TA1999-RG6:564 | (b) Trunked Radio Transceiver
-- src:TA1999-RG6:565 | (c) Mobile Data Transceiver
-- src:TA1999-RG6:566 | (d) Cordless Telephone (CT2/CT3)
-- src:TA1999-RG6:567 | 2. Analogue Cellular Mobile Phone $1,500 $750
-- src:TA1999-RG6:568 | (AMPS/ETACS)
-- src:TA1999-RG6:569 | 3. Radio Pager/Two-way Pager $1,300 $650
-- src:TA1999-RG6:570 | 4. Amateur Radio Transceiver $1,000 $500
-- src:TA1999-RG6:571 | 5. Dual-Band Digital Cellular Mobile Phone $570 $285
-- src:TA1999-RG6:572 | 6. Digital Cellular Mobile Phone $350 $175
-- src:TA1999-RG6:573 | (GSM/DCS/CDMA)
-- src:TA1999-RG6:574 | 7. Digital Cordless Telephone (DECT/PHS) $350 $ 175
-- src:TA1999-RG6:575 | (Fixed or Mobile)
-- src:TA1999-RG6:576 | 8. Wireless LAN Transceiver $350 $175
-- src:TA1999-RG6:577 | 9. Low Power Device $350 $175
-- src:TA1999-RG6:578 | 10. Low Power Device (where testing by the $460 $230.
-- src:TA1999-RG6:579 | Authority is required)
@ref Rg 6 Fourth Schedule (src:TA1999-RG6:528-579)
GIVEN `type of equipment` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF NUMBER)
`Rg 6 Fourth Schedule (2004 Revised Edition): the application fee and the modification or re-test fee in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `type of equipment` EQUALS "Call Switching System/Multiplex System" THEN JUST (LIST 1200, 600)
           IF `type of equipment` EQUALS "Complex Terminal Equipment" THEN JUST (LIST 900, 450)
           IF `type of equipment` EQUALS "Telephone/Telephone Line Interface/Telephone Ancillary/Autodialler/Auto Answering Set/Security Alarm System/Modem/EFTPOS/CCAT" THEN JUST (LIST 700, 350)
           IF `type of equipment` EQUALS "Caller Identification Device/Fax Transceiver/Fax Modem/Telex Equipment/Digital Leased Circuit Equipment" THEN JUST (LIST 900, 450)
           IF `type of equipment` EQUALS "Analogue Radio-communication Equipment" THEN JUST (LIST 2000, 1000)
           IF `type of equipment` EQUALS "Analogue Cellular Mobile Phone (AMPS/ETACS)" THEN JUST (LIST 1500, 750)
           IF `type of equipment` EQUALS "Radio Pager/Two-way Pager" THEN JUST (LIST 1300, 650)
           IF `type of equipment` EQUALS "Amateur Radio Transceiver" THEN JUST (LIST 1000, 500)
           IF `type of equipment` EQUALS "Dual-Band Digital Cellular Mobile Phone" THEN JUST (LIST 570, 285)
           IF `type of equipment` EQUALS "Digital Cellular Mobile Phone (GSM/DCS/CDMA)" THEN JUST (LIST 350, 175)
           IF `type of equipment` EQUALS "Digital Cordless Telephone (DECT/PHS) (Fixed or Mobile)" THEN JUST (LIST 350, 175)
           IF `type of equipment` EQUALS "Wireless LAN Transceiver" THEN JUST (LIST 350, 175)
           IF `type of equipment` EQUALS "Low Power Device" THEN JUST (LIST 350, 175)
           IF `type of equipment` EQUALS "Low Power Device (where testing by the Authority is required)" THEN JUST (LIST 460, 230)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:TA1999-RG6:581 | FIFTH SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-RG6:582 | Regulation 22 (2)
-- src:TA1999-RG6:584 | FEES FOR TESTS DONE ON EQUIPMENT FOR PERSONAL USE
-- src:TA1999-RG6:586 | First column Second column Third column
-- src:TA1999-RG6:587 | Type of telecommunication equipment Test fee Re-test fee
-- src:TA1999-RG6:588 | LINE-BASED EQUIPMENT
-- src:TA1999-RG6:589 | 1. Standard Telephone $ 50 $ 25
-- src:TA1999-RG6:590 | 2. Modem $ 50 $ 25
-- src:TA1999-RG6:591 | 3. Call Switching/Multiplex System $500 $250
-- src:TA1999-RG6:592 | 4. Other Terminal Equipment $200 $100
-- src:TA1999-RG6:595 | RADIO-COMMUNICATION EQUIPMENT
-- src:TA1999-RG6:596 | 1. Cellular Mobile Phone $ 50 $ 25
-- src:TA1999-RG6:597 | 2. Cordless Telephone $ 50 $ 25
-- src:TA1999-RG6:598 | 3. Amateur Radio Transceiver $ 50 $ 25
-- src:TA1999-RG6:599 | 4. Low Power Device $ 55 $ 28
-- src:TA1999-RG6:600 | 5. Wireless LAN Transceiver $ 55 $ 28
-- src:TA1999-RG6:601 | 6. Other Radio-communication Equipment $200 $100.
@ref Rg 6 Fifth Schedule (2004 Revised Edition) (src:TA1999-RG6:581-601)
GIVEN `type of equipment` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF NUMBER)
`Rg 6 Fifth Schedule (2004 Revised Edition): the test fee and the re-test fee in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `type of equipment` EQUALS "Standard Telephone" THEN JUST (LIST 50, 25)
           IF `type of equipment` EQUALS "Modem" THEN JUST (LIST 50, 25)
           IF `type of equipment` EQUALS "Call Switching/Multiplex System" THEN JUST (LIST 500, 250)
           IF `type of equipment` EQUALS "Other Terminal Equipment" THEN JUST (LIST 200, 100)
           IF `type of equipment` EQUALS "Cellular Mobile Phone" THEN JUST (LIST 50, 25)
           IF `type of equipment` EQUALS "Cordless Telephone" THEN JUST (LIST 50, 25)
           IF `type of equipment` EQUALS "Amateur Radio Transceiver (radio-communication)" THEN JUST (LIST 50, 25)
           IF `type of equipment` EQUALS "Low Power Device (radio-communication)" THEN JUST (LIST 55, 28)
           IF `type of equipment` EQUALS "Wireless LAN Transceiver (radio-communication)" THEN JUST (LIST 55, 28)
           IF `type of equipment` EQUALS "Other Radio-communication Equipment" THEN JUST (LIST 200, 100)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING
